version pl92_603_v
  cite pl92_603
  governs always
  known 1972-10-30
  note "known: the Act's approval date (law from approval, §4.5). Which act: its Sec. 102(e)(1) rewrote §202(q)(1)(A), inserting provisions for widow's and widower's benefits, and so gave the cited clause its present wording (US Code notes to 42 U.S.C. 402, 1972 amendments). Pub. L. 103-296 Sec. 321(a)(3) (1994) only struck a dash after 'multiplied by', which keeps the wording. The 5/9-of-1-percent fraction itself dates from the 1956 amendments (women) and Pub. L. 87-64 (men, 1961); round 2 cited the 1961 Act. SSA's compilation of §202 (Wayback capture 2024-12-12) is the locator only (§5.3)"
  early_pct_1 = 1/180 "§202(q)(1)(A): 5/9 of 1 percent of such amount if such benefit is an old-age insurance benefit (SSA compilation of §202)"

version pl95_216_v
  cite pl95_216
  governs always
  known 1977-12-20
  note "known: the Act's approval date (law from approval, §4.5). Which act: the US Code notes to 42 U.S.C. 415 show no later change to §215(a)(1)(A)(i)-(iii); Pub. L. 97-35 (1981) reworded only the rounding words after clause (iii). Its Title II rewrote §215(a) with the 90/32/15 percent formula; the leaflets restate it ('How it works'). SSA's pre-repeal compilation of §215 (Wayback capture 2024-12-02) is the locator only (§5.3)"
  pia_pct[t1] = 0.9 "§215(a)(1)(A)(i), 90 percent; leaflets p. 1 'How it works': × 90%"
  pia_pct[t2] = 0.32 "§215(a)(1)(A)(ii), 32 percent; leaflets: × 32%"
  pia_pct[t3] = 0.15 "§215(a)(1)(A)(iii), 15 percent; leaflets: balance × 15%"

version pl98_21_v
  cite pl98_21
  governs always
  known 1983-04-20
  note "known: the Act's approval date (law from approval, §4.5). It enacted the WEP, §215(a)(7) (Sec. 113, 'Elimination of windfall benefits for individuals receiving pensions from noncovered employment'; SSA POMS RS 00605.360), the 5/12-of-1-percent reduction beyond 36 months (§202(q)(9), Sec. 201(b)(1)) and the 2/3-of-1-percent delayed credit for eligibility after 2004 (§202(w)(6), Sec. 114(b)). Which act: the US Code notes to 42 U.S.C. 402 and 415 show no later change to the wording of §202(q)(9)(A), §202(w)(6)(D) or §215(a)(7)(B)(ii)(V); Pub. L. 103-296 touched only (q)(9)'s opening words and (q)(9)(B), and Pub. L. 98-369 only (a)(7)(B)(ii)(I). The other WEP rows sit with the later acts that reworded their text: (D)'s table with Pub. L. 100-647, its 30-year sentence with Pub. L. 101-508, and (A) with Pub. L. 103-296. As enacted here, (D) eased the cut only from 26 years (97 Stat. 77). SSA's compilations of §202 (Wayback 2024-12-12) and of §215 before the repeal (Wayback 2024-12-02) are the locators only (§5.3); the leaflets' p. 2 second table prints the same percentages"
  drc_pct = 1/150 "§202(w)(6)(D): 2/3 of 1 percent, first eligible after 2004"
  early_cut = 36 "§202(q)(9)(A): the first 36 months"
  early_pct_2 = 1/240 "§202(q)(9)(A): five-twelfths of 1 percent"
  wep_pct[0..20] = 0.4 "§215(a)(7)(B)(ii)(V): 40.0 percent for eligibility in 1990 or later; leaflets p. 2 second table, 20 or fewer, 40%"

version pl100_647_v
