version pl101_508_v
  cite pl101_508
  governs always
  known 1990-11-05
  note "known: the Act's approval date (law from approval, §4.5). Which act: its Sec. 5122(b) struck '(as defined in paragraph (1)(C)(ii))' from the end of §215(a)(7)(D)'s first sentence, which exempts 30 or more years of coverage, and added the sentence that reads a year of coverage at 25 percent; so it gave the cited sentence its present wording (US Code notes to 42 U.S.C. 415, 1990 amendments). Pub. L. 98-21 enacted the exemption itself. SSA's compilation of §215 before the repeal (Wayback 2024-12-02) is the locator only (§5.3)"
