,9:I:M:UL-15,11:checks-plan,34:run integration/models/UL-15.tally,24542:30:integration/models/UL-15.tally,24501:model ul15
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "Polish PIT 2022 for a person with two employments, or a pension and an employment (Ministerstwo Finansów, Rozliczenie PIT: zwroty i dopłaty podatku za 2022 r., 'Dopłaty podatku'; the same figures on slides 16 and 17 of the attached presentation of 9 February 2023)."
  note "The payment due in the return (dopłata) is the tax due for 2022 less the advances the payers collected. The advances are counted per payer, month by month. January to June ran under the 'rolowanie' rules, July to December at 12% (Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265 art. 23 ust. 1)."
  note "The page gives neither the advances nor the annual tax, and several facts and rules they rest on are not in the sources: the January-June rolowanie regulation, the social insurance rate, which payer applied the 1/12 reduction, the scale and the ulga dla pracowników in their wording of 30 June 2022 (Dz.U. 2021 poz. 2105) that the hypothetical tax of art. 26 reads through a wording pin, and the 2021 rules. Each is a hole with its question, and the steps around it are written, so the dopłata and the gain against 2021 are holes until they are given."
  note "Not modelled: the health contribution (not deductible from tax in 2022), the annual cap on social insurance contributions (no example reaches it), and the ulga dla pracowników in January-June advances, which sits inside the rolowanie hole."

source lifted_1_0_1 "Figures tally 1.0.1 allowed inline in rules"

source mf_page "Ministerstwo Finansów, Rozliczenie PIT: zwroty i dopłaty podatku za 2022 r. (14.02.2023)" at "https://www.gov.pl/web/finanse/rozliczenie-pit-zwroty-i-doplaty-podatku-za-2022-r"

source modeller "The model's own readings and assumptions, each stated with its reason"

source ustawa_1265 "Ustawa z dnia 9 czerwca 2022 r. o zmianie ustawy o podatku dochodowym od osób fizycznych oraz niektórych innych ustaw, Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265 (Warszawa, dnia 15 czerwca 2022 r.)" at "https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/DU/2022/1265/text.pdf"

source ustawa_2011_1707 "Ustawa z dnia 22 grudnia 2011 r. o zmianie niektórych ustaw związanych z realizacją ustawy budżetowej, Dz.U. 2011 nr 291 poz. 1707 (published 30 December 2011), art. 4 pkt 1: new wording of art. 63 § 1 of the Ordynacja podatkowa; the wording is the same in the tekst jednolity, Dz.U. 2021 poz. 1540 (p. 43)" at "https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/DU/2011/1707/text.pdf"

source ustawa_2019_1835 "Ustawa z dnia 30 sierpnia 2019 r. o zmianie ustawy o podatku dochodowym od osób fizycznych oraz ustawy o zmianie ustawy o podatku dochodowym od osób fizycznych oraz niektórych innych ustaw, Dz.U. 2019 poz. 1835 (Warszawa, dnia 26 września 2019 r.), art. 1 pkt 1: new wording of art. 22 ust. 2 of the PIT act; the wording is the same in the tekst jednolity, Dz.U. 2022 poz. 2647 (p. 78)" at "https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/DU/2019/1835/text.pdf"

source ustawa_2021_2105 "Ustawa z dnia 29 października 2021 r. o zmianie ustawy o podatku dochodowym od osób fizycznych, ustawy o podatku dochodowym od osób prawnych oraz niektórych innych ustaw, Dz.U. 2021 poz. 2105 (Warszawa, dnia 23 listopada 2021 r.); not one of the case's sources" at "https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/DU/2021/2105/text.pdf"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

axis ul15_hypo
  apart "the dopłata is the return's own figure; a refund under art. 26 of Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265 is paid by the tax office apart from it"
  netted "the dopłata shown is net of the art. 26 refund of the excess over the hypothetical tax"

index ex = [ex_a, ex_b, ex_c, ex_d, ex_e, ex_p1, ex_p2, ex_p3, ex_p4]

index mon = month 2022-01..2022-12

index srcs = [job1, job2, pension]

input adv_r_h2: num

input amount_m[e in ex, s in srcs]: money PLN
  note "The monthly amount from this source: an employment, or the pension; '-' where the example has no such source."

input commuter[e in ex, s in srcs]: bool question "Did this employer apply the higher costs for an employee living outside the town of the workplace (art. 22 ust. 2 pkt 3-4)?"

input cost_cap1: money PLN

input cost_cap2: money PLN

input cost_m: money PLN

input costs_y_2: int
  note "lifted from an inline figure of tally 1.0.1"

input full_year[e in ex, s in srcs]: bool question "Was this source paid at the same amount in each of the twelve months of 2022?"

input gross[e in ex]: bool question "Are the example's monthly amounts gross (brutto) pay?"

input hypo_hi: money PLN

input hypo_lo: money PLN

input pit2[e in ex, s in srcs]: bool question "Did this payer reduce each advance by 1/12 of the kwota zmniejszająca podatek (PIT-2 statement, art. 32 ust. 3 pkt 5; for a pension, the organ rentowy)?"

input pit_kz: money PLN

input pit_r1: num

input pit_r2: num

input pit_t2: money PLN

input reduction_12: int
  note "lifted from an inline figure of tally 1.0.1"

input wording_day: date
input zus_rate: num question "What share of the gross pay are the employee's social insurance contributions (emerytalne, rentowe, chorobowe) that the employer deducts (art. 26 ust. 1 pkt 2; art. 32 ust. 2)?"

band pit_scale(x: money PLN): num PLN
  note "Art. 27 ust. 1, the scale. Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265 gives it for income from 1 January 2022 (art. 18 ust. 1). Its wording of 30 June 2022, from Dz.U. 2021 poz. 2105, is read only by the hypothetical tax, through the wording pin of hypo_tax."

def adv[e in ex, s in srcs, m in mon]: money PLN at start_of(m)
  note "The advance collected by this payer for the month, rounded to whole złoty (Ordynacja podatkowa art. 63 § 1)."
  rule base v op63 = round(adv_raw[e, s, m], 1, half-up)

def adv_base[e in ex, s in srcs, m in mon]: money PLN at start_of(m)
  note "The month's income at this payer, the base of the advance, rounded to whole złoty (art. 63 § 1)."
  rule base v op63 = round(inc_m[e, s, m], 1, half-up)

def adv_raw[e in ex, s in srcs, m in mon]: num PLN at start_of(m)
  note "January-June: the payer computed the advance under the 2022 and the 2021 rules and collected the lower ('rolowanie'). July-December: art. 32 ust. 1 in its wording before Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265, at 12% instead of 17%, less the monthly reduction (art. 32 ust. 3; Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265 art. 23 ust. 1 and 4). An advance doesn't go below zero."
  note "Art. 32 ust. 1 changes the rate once the income from the start of the year at one payer passes the upper end of the scale's first row, read here as band_hi(pit_scale, 0). The rule tests the revenue, which is never below the income, so it raises its hole whenever the income could pass."
  rule h1 v mf_rolowanie = ?"What advance did this payer collect in this month of January-June 2022? The rolowanie regulation (the lower of the advance under the 2022 and the 2021 rules) is not in the sources."
  rule h2 v law_1265_h2 = max(0, adv_r_h2 * adv_base[e, s, m] - reduction[e, s, m])
  rule upper beats h1, h2 = ?"Above the upper end of the scale's first row (120 000 zł) of income at one payer, the advance is 32% of the excess (art. 32 ust. 1). That part is not written, and no example reaches it." when cum_rev[e, s, m] > band_hi(pit_scale, 0)

def adv_total[e in ex]: num PLN = sum(sum(adv[e, s, m] for m in mon) for s in srcs where amount_m[e, s] != none) at reader

def cost_month[e in ex, s in srcs, m in mon]: num PLN at start_of(m)
  note "Art. 22 ust. 2 pkt 1: 250 zł a month for each employment; a pension has none."
  rule base = cost_m
  rule far beats base = ?"The costs of a commuting employee (300 zł a month, art. 22 ust. 2 pkt 3-4) are not written." when s != pension and commuter[e, s]
  rule pension beats base = 0 when s == pension

def costs_y[e in ex]: num PLN at reader
  note "The annual employment costs in the return: art. 22 ust. 2 pkt 1 caps one employment at 3000 zł; pkt 2 caps several employments together at 4500 zł."
  rule far beats one, several = ?"The annual cap for commuting employees (3600 zł or 5400 zł, art. 22 ust. 2 pkt 3-4) is not written." when any(commuter[e, s] for s in srcs where s != pension and amount_m[e, s] != none)
  rule nojob = 0 when n_jobs[e] == 0
  rule one = min(cost_cap1, job_costs[e]) when n_jobs[e] == 1
  rule several = min(cost_cap2, job_costs[e]) when n_jobs[e] >= costs_y_2

def cum_rev[e in ex, s in srcs, m in mon]: num PLN = sum(rev_m[e, s, k] for k in mon where k <= m) at start_of(m)

def doplata[e in ex]: num PLN at reader
  note "The payment due in the return: the tax due less the advances. A negative value would be a refund."
  rule apart = tax_due[e] - adv_total[e] when ul15_hypo == apart
  rule netted = tax_due[e] - adv_total[e] - hypo_refund[e] when ul15_hypo == netted

def gain[e in ex]: num PLN at reader
  note "The page's 'roczna korzyść w stosunku do 2021 r.' and 'podatek niższy niż w 2021 r.': the 2021 tax less the 2022 tax."
  rule base = tax_2021[e] - tax_due[e]

def hypo_refund[e in ex]: num PLN at reader
  note "Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265 art. 26 ust. 1-2: for employment or business revenue from 68 412 zł to 133 692 zł, the tax office refunds the excess of the 2022 tax over the hypothetical tax."
  rule base = 0
  rule inband beats base v law_1265_a26 = max(0, tax_due[e] - hypo_tax[e]) when in_band[e]

def hypo_tax[e in ex]: num PLN at reader
  note "Art. 26 ust. 3 of Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265: the tax for 2022 on the same revenue under the PIT act as that act amended it, but with the ulga dla pracowników (art. 26 ust. 1 pkt 2aa) and the scale (art. 27 ust. 1) in their wording of 30 June 2022. So it is tax_due with the items that hold the relief and the scale read in the wording in force on that day. Poz. 1265 enters into force on 1 July 2022, so the pin passes over it to Dz.U. 2021 poz. 2105, whose scale row and relief rule are holes here; every law date stays 2022's."
  rule base v law_1265_a26 = tax_due[e] as if {wording wording_day for [pit_kz, pit_r1, pit_r2, pit_scale, pit_t2, ulga_prac]}

def in_band[e in ex]: bool = job_rev[e] >= hypo_lo and job_rev[e] <= hypo_hi at reader

def inc_m[e in ex, s in srcs, m in mon]: num PLN at start_of(m)
  note "Art. 32 ust. 2: the month's revenue at this payer less the employment costs and the social insurance contributions deducted that month."
  rule base = rev_m[e, s, m] - cost_month[e, s, m] - zus_m[e, s, m]

def income_y[e in ex]: num PLN at reader
  note "The annual income on the scale: revenue less employment costs (art. 22 ust. 2) and less the social insurance contributions (art. 26 ust. 1 pkt 2)."
  rule base = sum(rev_y[e, s] - zus_y[e, s] for s in srcs where amount_m[e, s] != none) - costs_y[e]

def job_costs[e in ex]: num PLN = sum(sum(cost_month[e, s, m] for m in mon) for s in srcs where s != pension and amount_m[e, s] != none) at reader

def job_rev[e in ex]: money PLN at reader
  note "Art. 26 ust. 2 of Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265 counts employment and business revenue, not pensions."
  rule base = sum(rev_y[e, s] for s in srcs where s != pension and amount_m[e, s] != none)

def n_jobs[e in ex]: int = count(s in srcs where s != pension and amount_m[e, s] != none) at reader

def reduction[e in ex, s in srcs, m in mon]: num PLN at start_of(m)
  note "Art. 32 ust. 3: 1/12 of the kwota zmniejszająca podatek, at the payer named in the PIT-2 statement."
  rule base = 0
  rule pit2 beats base = pit_kz / reduction_12 when pit2[e, s]

def rev_m[e in ex, s in srcs, m in mon]: money PLN at start_of(m)
  note "The month's gross revenue from this source."
  rule base = amount_m[e, s]
  rule netpay beats base = ?"The monthly amounts are not gross pay; the gross is not given." when not gross[e]
  rule partyear beats base, netpay = ?"Which months of 2022 was this source paid, and at what amount?" when not full_year[e, s]

def rev_y[e in ex, s in srcs]: money PLN = sum(rev_m[e, s, m] for m in mon) at reader

def tax_2021[e in ex]: num PLN at reader
  note "The tax for 2021 that the page compares with."
  rule base = ?"What would this person's tax for 2021 have been on the same pay? The 2021 rules and the assumptions behind the page's comparison are not in the sources."

def tax_base[e in ex]: money PLN at reader
  note "The annual income less the ulga dla pracowników (art. 26 ust. 1 pkt 2aa; none in the return for 2022, see ulga_prac), rounded to whole złoty (Ordynacja podatkowa art. 63 § 1)."
  rule base v op63 = round(income_y[e] - ulga_prac[e], 1, half-up)

def tax_due[e in ex]: money PLN at reader
  note "The scale on the base, rounded to whole złoty (art. 63 § 1); the scale gives no negative tax."
  rule base v op63 = round(max(0, pit_scale(tax_base[e])), 1, half-up)

def ulga_prac[e in ex]: num PLN at reader
  note "Art. 26 ust. 1 pkt 2aa and ust. 4a-4c: the ulga dla pracowników, deducted from income. Dz.U. 2021 poz. 2105 added it for income from 2022. Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265 repealed it (art. 1 pkt 10 lit. a, p. 4) and doesn't apply it to income from 1 January 2022 (art. 18 ust. 2, p. 21), so the return for 2022 has none. The hypothetical tax reads it in its wording of 30 June 2022 (hypo_tax)."
  rule base v law_2105 = ?"What is the ulga dla pracowników of art. 26 ust. 1 pkt 2aa and ust. 4a-4c, in the wording of Dz.U. 2021 poz. 2105 in force on 30 June 2022, on this person's 2022 employment revenue? That text is not among the case's sources."

def zus_m[e in ex, s in srcs, m in mon]: num PLN at start_of(m)
  note "The employee's social insurance contributions deducted by the employer; none on a pension."
  rule base = zus_rate * rev_m[e, s, m]
  rule pension beats base = 0 when s == pension

def zus_y[e in ex, s in srcs]: num PLN = sum(zus_m[e, s, m] for m in mon) at reader

ask q01_doplata: doplata[e] for e in ex law 2022-12-31

ask q02_gain: gain[e] for e in ex law 2022-12-31

ask q03_job_rev: job_rev[e] for e in ex law 2022-12-31

ask q04_in_band: in_band[e] for e in ex law 2022-12-31

ask q05_costs: costs_y[e] for e in ex law 2022-12-31

ask q06_adv_july: adv[e, s, m] for e in ex, s in srcs where amount_m[e, s] != none, m in [2022-07] law 2026-10-18

version lifted_figures
  cite lifted_1_0_1
  governs always
  known 2011-12-30
  costs_y_2 = 2 "inline in tally 1.0.1: costs_y line 95, operand"
  reduction_12 = 12 "inline in tally 1.0.1: reduction line 138, factor"

version op63
  cite ustawa_2011_1707
  governs 2012-03-31..
  known 2011-12-30
  note "Known from the act's publication in the Dziennik Ustaw, 30 December 2011 (ELI record https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/DU/2011/1707: promulgation 2011-12-30). Art. 41 pkt 2: art. 4 enters into force three months after publication, so the wording governs from 31 March 2012, which is also its default enters."
  note "Art. 4 pkt 1 (p. 16895), art. 63 § 1: 'Podstawy opodatkowania, kwoty podatków ... zaokrągla się do pełnych złotych w ten sposób, że końcówki kwot wynoszące mniej niż 50 groszy pomija się, a końcówki kwot wynoszące 50 i więcej groszy podwyższa się do pełnych złotych'. The tekst jednolity Dz.U. 2021 poz. 1540 prints § 1 word for word as this act gave it, so no later act restated it."

version law_1835
  cite ustawa_2019_1835
  governs 2020..
  known 2019-09-26
  note "Known from the act's publication, 26 September 2019. Art. 7 ust. 2 (p. 3): the new art. 22 ust. 2 applies to income from 1 January 2020. Art. 1 pkt 1 enters into force on 1 January 2020 (ELI record https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/DU/2019/1835: 'art. 1 pkt 1-3 i 5, art. 2 i art. 7 ust. 2 wchodzą w życie z dniem 1 stycznia 2020'), which is the default enters."
  note "Art. 22 ust. 2 pkt 3-4, the commuters' 300 zł a month, 3600 zł and 5400 zł a year, are not rows: the model assumes no commuting."
  cost_cap1 = 3000 "art. 1 pkt 1 (p. 1), art. 22 ust. 2 pkt 1: 'za rok podatkowy łącznie nie więcej niż 3000 zł'"
  cost_cap2 = 4500 "art. 1 pkt 1 (p. 1), art. 22 ust. 2 pkt 2: 'nie mogą przekroczyć łącznie 4500 zł za rok podatkowy'"
  cost_m = 250 "art. 1 pkt 1 (p. 1), art. 22 ust. 2 pkt 1: 'wynoszą 250 zł miesięcznie'"

version law_2105
  cite ustawa_2021_2105
  governs 2022..
  known 2021-11-23
  note "Known from the act's publication in the Dziennik Ustaw, 23 November 2021 (its header 'Warszawa, dnia 23 listopada 2021 r.'; ELI record https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/DU/2021/2105: promulgation 2021-11-23). Art. 1 pkt 40 and 47 enter into force on 1 January 2022 (art. 89, p. 140, not among its exceptions), the default enters, and art. 70 (p. 137) applies them to income from 1 January 2022, so the version governs from 2022."
  note "This is the wording of 30 June 2022 that Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265 art. 26 ust. 3 names: art. 1 pkt 47 lit. a (p. 28) gave art. 27 ust. 1 its scale, and art. 1 pkt 40 lit. a and b (p. 19) added art. 26 ust. 1 pkt 2aa and ust. 4a-4c. It is the latest amendment of those provisions before that day that I found. I did not check each act of the first half of 2022 that amended the PIT act (poz. 1265, footnote 2), so the version takes this one as the latest amendment found."
  note "The act is not among the case's sources, so the model takes no figure from it; it was read only for its dates and locators. Its scale row is a hole, as is the rule ulga_prac.base that points here. Poz. 1265, known later, beats both for every reader of 2022; only the wording pin of hypo_tax reaches them."
  pit_scale: [0, inf) = ?"What is the scale of art. 27 ust. 1 in its wording of 30 June 2022 (Dz.U. 2021 poz. 2105, art. 1 pkt 47 lit. a)? The hypothetical tax of Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265 art. 26 ust. 3 pkt 2 uses it, and that text is not among the case's sources." "art. 1 pkt 47 lit. a (p. 28), art. 27 ust. 1"

version law_1265
  cite ustawa_1265
  governs 2022..
  known 2022-06-15
  enters 2022-07-01
  note "Known from the act's publication in the Dziennik Ustaw, 15 June 2022 (its header 'Warszawa, dnia 15 czerwca 2022 r.'). It enters into force on 1 July 2022 (art. 40, p. 26; ELI record https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/DU/2022/1265: entryIntoForce 2022-07-01). None of art. 40's exceptions covers what this version holds (art. 1 pkt 10 lit. a and pkt 13 lit. a, art. 18 ust. 1 and 2), so enters is 1 July 2022, not the default of 15 June."
  note "Art. 18 ust. 1 (p. 21): the new art. 27 ust. 1 applies to income from 1 January 2022, so the version governs from 2022. Art. 18 ust. 2 (p. 21): art. 26 ust. 1 pkt 2aa in its earlier wording does not apply to income from 1 January 2022; the rule ulga_prac.base points here."
  wording_day = 2022-06-30 governs always "art. 26 ust. 3: the wording of 30 June 2022"
  pit_kz = 3600 "art. 1 pkt 13 lit. a (p. 5), art. 27 ust. 1, tabela, wiersz 1: 'minus kwota zmniejszająca podatek 3600 zł'"
  pit_r1 = 0.12 "art. 1 pkt 13 lit. a (p. 5), art. 27 ust. 1, tabela, wiersz 1: '12%'"
  pit_r2 = 0.32 "art. 1 pkt 13 lit. a (p. 5), art. 27 ust. 1, tabela, wiersz 2: '32% nadwyżki ponad 120 000 zł'"
  replace pit_scale: [0, 120000] = x * pit_r1 - pit_kz "art. 1 pkt 13 lit. a (p. 5), art. 27 ust. 1, tabela, wiersz 1 'do 120 000'"
  replace pit_scale: (120000, inf) = pit_t2 + (x - band_lo(pit_scale, x)) * pit_r2 "art. 1 pkt 13 lit. a (p. 5), art. 27 ust. 1, tabela, wiersz 2 'ponad 120 000': '10 800 zł + 32% nadwyżki ponad 120 000 zł'"
  pit_t2 = 10800 "art. 1 pkt 13 lit. a (p. 5), art. 27 ust. 1, tabela, wiersz 2: '10 800 zł'"
  replace rule ulga_prac.base v law_1265 = 0

version law_1265_a26
  cite ustawa_1265
  governs 2022
  known 2022-06-15
  enters 2023-01-01
  note "Known from the act's publication, 15 June 2022. Art. 26 enters into force on 1 January 2023 (art. 40 pkt 3, p. 26), apart from the rest of the act, and sets the refund for the tax for 2022, so this version governs 2022 and enters on 1 January 2023. The rules hypo_tax.base and hypo_refund.inband point here."
  note "Art. 26 ust. 3 (p. 23): 'Hipotetyczny podatek należny za 2022 r. oblicza się od przychodów uzyskanych w 2022 r. zgodnie z przepisami ustawy zmienianej w art. 1, w brzmieniu nadanym niniejszą ustawą, przy czym: 1) uwzględnia się ulgę dla pracowników ..., o której mowa w art. 26 ust. 1 pkt 2aa ... w brzmieniu z dnia 30 czerwca 2022 r. ...; 2) uwzględnia się skalę podatkową, o której mowa w art. 27 ust. 1 ..., w brzmieniu z dnia 30 czerwca 2022 r.'"
  hypo_hi = 133692 "art. 26 ust. 2 (p. 23): 'w wysokości od 68 412 zł do 133 692 zł'"
  hypo_lo = 68412 "art. 26 ust. 2 (p. 23): 'w wysokości od 68 412 zł do 133 692 zł'"

version law_1265_h2
  cite ustawa_1265
  governs 2022-07..2022-12
  known 2022-06-15
  note "Known from the act's publication, 15 June 2022. Art. 23 enters into force with the act on 1 July 2022 (art. 40), which is the default enters, the start of governs. Art. 23 ust. 4 (p. 22): from 1 July to 31 December 2022 the advance is not reduced by the ulga dla pracowników."
  adv_r_h2 = 0.12 "art. 23 ust. 1 (p. 22): 'od dochodów uzyskanych w okresie od dnia 1 lipca 2022 r. do dnia 31 grudnia 2022 r. zamiast stawki 17% stosuje się stawkę 12%'"

version mf_rolowanie
  cite mf_page
  governs 2022-01..2022-06
  known 2023-02-14
  note "Known from the page's first public release, its date line 14.02.2023; the page shows no later update (checked on 2026-10-19)."
  note "The page: in January-June 2022 'porównywano zaliczki obliczone wg zasad z 2022 r. i z 2021 r. i pobierano niższą z nich'. It stands for the rules on those advances, which it does not name: the Rozporządzenie Ministra Finansów z dnia 7 stycznia 2022 r. (Dz.U. 2022 poz. 28) and art. 53a of the PIT act in its wording before Dz.U. 2022 poz. 1265 (named in poz. 1265 art. 18 ust. 3 and art. 28). Neither is in the sources, and the page records no date for them, so the version is known at the page's own date. It has no rows; only the hole rule adv_raw.h1 points at it."

version facts_mf
  cite mf_page
  governs always
  known 2026-10-18
  note "The page's examples are hypothetical cases: their stipulations are known from the model's on (it has no start), not from the page's date."
  note "Section 'Dopłaty podatku'. The two-jobs examples are A to E, the working pensioners P1 to P4; slides 16 and 17 of the presentation give the same amounts."
  amount_m = none "the examples name only the sources below"
  amount_m[ex_a, job1] = 3000 "two-jobs paragraph: 'na jednym zarabia 3 tys. zł i na drugim też 3 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_a, job2] = 3000 "two-jobs paragraph: 'na jednym zarabia 3 tys. zł i na drugim też 3 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_b, job1] = 3000 "two-jobs paragraph: 'na jednym zarabia 3 tys. zł, a na drugim 4 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_b, job2] = 4000 "two-jobs paragraph: 'na jednym zarabia 3 tys. zł, a na drugim 4 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_c, job1] = 3000 "next paragraph: 'na pierwszym zarabia 3 tys. zł, a na drugim 6 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_c, job2] = 6000 "next paragraph: 'na pierwszym zarabia 3 tys. zł, a na drugim 6 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_d, job1] = 4000 "next paragraph: 'na pierwszym etacie zarabia 4 tys. zł, a na drugim 2 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_d, job2] = 2000 "next paragraph: 'na pierwszym etacie zarabia 4 tys. zł, a na drugim 2 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_e, job1] = 4000 "next paragraph: 'na pierwszym etacie zarabia 4 tys. zł, a na drugim 5 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_e, job2] = 5000 "next paragraph: 'na pierwszym etacie zarabia 4 tys. zł, a na drugim 5 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_p1, job1] = 1000 "pensioner paragraph: 'dorabiający na etacie 1 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_p1, pension] = 2500 "pensioner paragraph: 'ze świadczeniem 2,5 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_p2, job1] = 3000 "pensioner paragraph: 'wynagrodzenie 3 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_p2, pension] = 2500 "pensioner paragraph: 'świadczenie wynosi 2,5 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_p3, job1] = 6000 "pensioner paragraph: 'zarobkach na umowie o pracę wynoszących 6 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_p3, pension] = 2500 "pensioner paragraph: 'przy emeryturze wynoszącej 2,5 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_p4, job1] = 5000 "pensioner paragraph: 'wynagrodzenie 5 tys. zł'"
  amount_m[ex_p4, pension] = 2000 "pensioner paragraph: 'świadczenie wynosi 2 tys. zł'"

